# Every file here ends up either baked into a Linux container image (as a
# script executed by shebang) or read by tools inside one. A CRLF line
# ending silently breaks a shebang line ("#!/bin/sh\r" is not a valid
# interpreter path) and shows up as the container failing to start, not as
# a build error — confirmed live: this repo had no .gitattributes, so a
# checkout on Windows with the common core.autocrlf=true setting converted
# tracked LF blobs to CRLF in the working tree, and podman build copies
# from the working tree, not from git. Force LF unconditionally, regardless
# of any local core.autocrlf setting, so this can't recur on any platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
